<title>GREECE: OTE TELECOM FACILITATES SOLDIERS IN BOSNIA.</title>
<headline>OTE TELECOM FACILITATES SOLDIERS IN BOSNIA.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Hellenic Telecommunications Organization (OTE), , has provided Greek soldiers in Bosnia with cardphone facilities and a 24-hour telephone service, it said in a statement on Friday.</p>
<p>OTE recently installed two cardphones in Bosnia for the use of 320 Greek soldiers and other foreign army officials participating in the peace corps currently located in the area, it added.</p>
<p>A total of 1,500 phonecards are being sent to Bosnia, by OTE. --Margarita Sotiropoulou, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
